  "body": "Slice 2 of #3329: the 3D Finish takes a start point and an exit point on its Parallel pattern. Deburr is slice 1 (#4168). The 3D Pocket stays open.\n\n## Behaviour\n\n- `OpType::Finish3D` has the capability `PickCapability::Raster`, as the Face and the 5-Axis Parallel.\n- On the Parallel pattern, at any pass direction, a pick chooses a corner of the zigzag raster. The order law is the raster seam of #3330 (`finishing3d::raster_seam::order`):\n  - Start: the corner nearest the start pick. The pass order is reversed, or each pass runs the other way.\n  - Exit: the order whose last pass ends nearest the exit pick.\n- The cut geometry does not change. Only the order and the direction of the passes change. The links are planned again on the new order by the raster's own link laws.\n- New motion entry `finishing3d::finish_seamed` (the angled Parallel raster with the picks) and the check `finishing3d::raster_ends_kept`.\n- No pick: the arm calls the same generator as before. The path is byte-identical.\n- MCP: `edit_operation` sets the picks (the existing `picks` field). Its schema names \"3D Finish (the Parallel pattern only; ...)\". Undo and redo go through `EditOperationParams`.\n\n## Refusals (by name, never moved)\n\n1. A pick on any pattern but Parallel. Refused at the command door (`pick_refusal`) and again in the generator.\n2. A pick farther than 1.5 tool diameters from every corner, and an exit that the start's order cannot end at (the shared raster seam).\n3. A pick on a model with no shallow ground.\n4. A plunge column at the picked start, or a retract column at the picked exit, within the ball radius of the part. Exact: `support::column_clear` (segment-to-facet distance), no sampling.\n5. One rule for a moved corner (`raster_ends_kept`): the finished path is read again. Its first cut must land on the picked start corner, and its last feed must end on the picked exit corner. This closes the class \"a later stage moves a picked corner\". Today it catches:\n   - an exit when the waterline rings cut after the raster (motion);\n   - a corner that the area controls clip away (application, after the clip and the centre-cutting guard).\n\n## Mutations\n\nEach mutation was applied alone on head b377b0561 and then restored. Each turned the named tests red:\n\n| # | Mutation | Red tests |\n|---|---|---|\n| M1 | motion: skip `raster_ends_kept` after the rings | `multiaxis finish_seam::finish_with_waterlines_keeps_a_start_and_refuses_an_exit_by_name` |\n| M2 | app: skip the post-clip `raster_ends_kept` | `start_exit_shared finish3d::finish3d_refuses_an_impossible_pick_by_name` |\n| M3 | motion: `ends_clear` always `Ok` | both `finish_seam_tests` (2 of 2) |\n| M4 | app: remove the door refusal of another pattern | `finish3d::finish3d_picks_ride_edit_operation_and_another_pattern_is_refused_at_the_door` |\n| M5 | motion: remove the generator's pattern refusal | `finish_seam::finish_refuses_an_impossible_pick_by_name` |\n| M6 | app: the arm ignores the picks | `finish3d_starts_at_the_picked_corner...` and `finish3d_refuses_an_impossible_pick_by_name` |\n| M7 | motion: `raster_ends_kept` compares the exit with the start tip | 3 of 5 `finish_seam` tests |\n\n## Readings\n\n- With 90 and 30 degree passes on the floor-and-block fixture: a start at the automatic end and an exit at the automatic start both reverse the whole raster. The first cut lands exactly on the picked corner and the last feed ends exactly on the other corner (to 1e-9). The tool rises straight up.\n- Picks at the automatic corners give the automatic path, move for move.\n- Each move of each picked path keeps more than `R - 0.05` mm from every facet (exact segment-to-facet distance). Both moved columns keep the full radius.\n- Through `generate` on the 30 x 20 x 10 block (angle 90): a start at the far end of the first pass plunges at `(a.x, -a.y)`. An exit at the automatic start ends the cut there.\n- The same exit with the waterline rings on is refused (\"the waterline rings cut after the raster\"). An area offset of -6 mm with a start pick is refused (\"the area controls clip the raster\").\n- Both picks at one corner are refused by name. No exit is moved. This is the same rule that the Deburr fix (#4168) uses, written down in the decision file.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion --lib finishing3d::finish_seam_tests` (2): the exact column law, with a canopy, at the ball radius (3.000 passes, 2.999 is refused).\n- `camcraft-motion --test multiaxis finish_seam` (5): byte-identical without a pick at three angles; start, exit and both picks at 90 and 30 degrees (each cut sampled every 0.25 mm on the automatic raster and back; every move's ball segment checked exactly against each facet; both moved columns checked exactly); the waterline exit refusal; each pattern refusal; the moved-corner rule.\n- `camcraft-app --test start_exit_shared finish3d` (3): the started and exited raster through `generate` (far end of the first pass, the whole raster reversed, straight rise, top cuts sampled every 0.25 mm), the refusals (far pick, rings, area controls), MCP edit, the door refusal of another pattern, undo and redo, the schema text.\n- `start_exit_shared::every_kind_has_one_pick_capability...` now expects `Raster` for the 3D Finish.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No fixture, golden, recorded program or snapshot changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Picks on the other 3D Finish patterns: refused by name (see the decision file for why).\n- The UI has no 3D Finish start / exit rows yet, as for the 5-axis slices. The picks are set through MCP and the project file.\n- The full heavy lanes (P2: no heavy step).\n\n## Remaining kinds of #3329\n\n3D Pocket.\n\n## Gate\n\nMac lane (the Mac gate lock), head `61d5b61ed`. The first line of each log is that head.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 217 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 32.3 min. The plan holds `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, `golden_cl`, `start_exit_shared`, motion `lib` and `multiaxis`. All ok.\n  - Three earlier attempts on this head stopped at the first build step, before any test ran. The error was E0463 \"can't find crate\". The dependency metadata in this worktree's debug target was unreadable after the target folder changed outside this run (also without sccache). I deleted the worktree's `target/debug` and the fourth run passed. No code changed between the runs.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n- No heavy step (P2).\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3329-finish3d-picks.md`.\n\nChangelog: 3D Finish: a start point and an exit point choose the corner of the Parallel raster where the cut starts and where its last pass ends; a pick that the raster cannot keep is refused by name.\n\nEffort: max\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #3329\n",
